 To operate a car with a manual transmission, you need to use the clutch and the shifter to change gears. When starting the car, put it in first gear and gently press the clutch pedal while you slowly release the parking brake. Then, slowly move the shifter into second gear and continue to release the clutch pedal until you feel the engine revving up. Once you have reached the desired speed, you can release your foot from the clutch and move the shifter into a higher gear. When coming to a stop, depress the clutch pedal and move the shifter into neutral before releasing it. Finally, when you are ready to move off, press down on the accelerator while simultaneously releasing the clutch pedal. Good luck!<unk> 
